<title>USA: Marathon buys Chevron fields in Wyoming.</title>
<headline>Marathon buys Chevron fields in Wyoming.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marathon Oil Co said it has purchased Chevron Corp's Steamboat Butte and Pilot Butte fields in Fremont County, Wyoming, for undisclosed terms.</p>
<p>These properties produce 940 barrels of oil and 700,000 cubic feet of natural gas daily from 34 wells, Marathon said.</p>
<p>The company said the purchase enhances its existing operations, which include the Circle Ridge field acquired in 1995, on the Wind River Indian Reservation.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
